==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:US Silvercert1.jpg|thumb|right|A one-dollar note (US), front and back.]]

===Etymology===
Attested since the mid-16th century, from early {{bor|en|nl|daler}}, {{m|nl|daalder}}, from {{der|en|de|Taler}}, {{m|de|Thaler||dollar}}, from {{m|de|Sankt Joachimsthaler}}, literally “of {{w|Joachimstal}}”, the name for coins minted in {{cog|de|Sankt Joachimsthal||St. Joachim's Valley}} (now {{w|Jáchymov}}, Czech Republic). Ultimately from {{m|de|Joachim}} + {{m|de|Tal||valley}}. Possibly reinforced by the Dutch {{m|en|leeuwendaalder}}, which was also used in the American colonies. Cognate to {{cog|da|daler}}. {{doublet|en|taler|id1=currency}}.

